.TH SMARTCANCEL 1
.SH NAME
smartcancel \- safely select and cancel Slurm jobs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smartcancel
.RI FILTERS
.RI [ --dry-run ]
.RI [ --force ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Selects the current user's jobs using intersecting directory, name, regex, age, state, partition, stdin-pattern, and latest-job filters.
At least one selector is required.
.PP
Dependent jobs are recursively included by default.
Every job in the final expanded set is displayed before confirmation, and that same set is used for dry-run and execution.
.SH OPTIONS
.BR --this-dir ,
.BR --dir " " PATH ,
.BR --name " " NAME ,
.BR --contains " " TEXT ,
.BR --regex " " PATTERN ,
.BR --older-than " " DURATION ,
.BR --younger-than " " DURATION ,
.BR --time-left " " DURATION ,
.BR --state " " STATE ,
.BR --partition " " NAME[,NAME...] ,
.BR --latest ,
.BR --dry-run ,
and
.BR --force .
.PP
.B --younger-than
and
.B --time-left
use strict less-than comparisons.
Non-numeric remaining-time values such as NOT_SET and UNLIMITED are excluded.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The keys
.BR confirm ,
.BR dry_run ,
and
.B smartcancel.include_dependents
are supported.
See the project configuration documentation for precedence and accepted boolean values.
